			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851904">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP article/Personnel profile</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Standard SCP page</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch:</p>
<ul>
<li>Our senses define and limit how we interact with reality, they do not, however, define and limit reality itself. (aka there is more around us than meet the eye)</li>
<li>Human eyes can perceive three colors of light: red, blue and green, other colors are perceived by combining these three with the intensity of the light. Other animals have different light perception and therefore can see different colors than humans. Particularly, praying mantis shrimps can perceive between 12 and 16 light colors.</li>
<li>What happens when a human receives an experimental implant that allows them to see as many colors as a praying mantis shrimp?</li>
</ul>
<p>Central Narrative: A high level MTF agent becomes blind after a mission and becomes the perfect guinea pig for an experimental biological implant that combines human and animal DNA to create augmented agents. The article starts with a brief description of the agent and how she lost her eyesight and how the implant was created. It follows with some logs regarding the surgery and recovery of the agent.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The meat of the narrative, though, is how her new eyes allow her to experience reality in a completely different way. Through personal entries on a journal she details her discoveries, they start small (new colors, night vision) and as she grows used to the new eyes they get bigger (she can see the flow of energy on living beings, see cracks and passages on reality that allow her to &quot;teleport&quot;, see time as it passes, etc).</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</p>
<ul>
<li>One goal here is create a new character to be used in future works on the wiki, she would make a great spy or extraction agent for example</li>
<li>Explore the growing sense of amazement and thrill someone feels when emerged on a new reality (aka my feelings when I discovered the SCP and plunged into this weird universe)</li>
<li>Expanding concepts such as the integrity of reality, time, space and other basic elements of the SCP universe and how humans and other beings interact with them</li>
</ul>
<p>Additional Notes: None so far. Let the critiques begin!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
